(@ extends 'base-booklet.jtex' @)

(@ set target = 'booklet' @)

(@ block colophon @)
(# The last page carries the credits, and the colophon is that page's footer rather than a
        block of body text above it -- `blocks/colophon.jtex` says what is in it, and
        `blocks/booklet/footer.jtex` asks for the style once the credits are laid down.

        **It is boxed here and used there**, which is what keeps the two halves of the
        arrangement in step. A footer grows *upward* from its baseline, so the colophon rises
        into the gap between the credits and the footrule -- and the credits are seated flush
        with the bottom of the text block, so without a reservation the rule cut through the
        last name on the page. The reservation is this box's own height rather than a length
        somebody measured off a proof: resize the type or add a row and the gap follows.
        `\thepage` stays outside the box, because a page number frozen in the preamble would
        print whatever page the box was built on.

        Only the centre field changes, so the style inherits the one the booklet ends in: the
        running head on that page still belongs to the last section, and a `colophon` built on
        `naboj` would drop the `Výsledky` beside the logo. fancyhdr 4's optional base argument
        is what makes that one line rather than a copy of the section style. #)
    \newsavebox{\dgsColophonBox}
    \newlength{\dgsColophonRise}
    (# How far the colophon is lifted above the page number's baseline, as against
        `\dgsColophonRise`, which is how much room the credits must leave free. They are
        different numbers and conflating them puts the colophon a box-height too high: the
        reservation is the colophon's whole vertical extent plus the gap, while the lift only
        has to clear the depth of its own last line and then the gap. #)
    \newlength{\dgsColophonLift}
    (# The gap **above** the colophon, between it and the rule. Deliberately the smaller of the
        two: the colophon belongs to the rule over it, not to the footer line under it, or the
        three read as one block of small print instead of as a colophon between a rule and a
        footer. `\dgsColophonFootGap` below is the other one. #)
    \newlength{\dgsColophonGap}
    \setlength{\dgsColophonGap}{3mm}
    (# The gap **below** the colophon, which is a different number from the one above it. The
        rule, the colophon and the footer line are three things stacked in one band, and they
        have to read as a colophon under a rule and over a footer rather than as one block of
        small print -- so the colophon is tied more closely to the rule above it than to the
        line below. 3mm alone left 0.3pt of clear air between the licence and the page number:
        measured, not eyeballed, and they all but touched.

        It is measured to the **bottom of the box**, which since the colophon became two
        columns is the logo's lower edge rather than the last line of small print -- the text
        is the shorter column and floats against the logo's middle, so the air under the last
        line it sets is this gap plus whatever centring left over it. #)
    \newlength{\dgsColophonFootGap}
    \setlength{\dgsColophonFootGap}{\dimexpr\dgsColophonGap + 0.6em + 2mm\relax}
    \AtBeginDocument{%
        \sbox{\dgsColophonBox}{%
            \parbox{\textwidth}{\centering (@ include 'blocks/colophon.jtex' @)}%
        }%
        \setlength{\dgsColophonRise}{%
            \dimexpr\ht\dgsColophonBox + \dp\dgsColophonBox + \dgsColophonFootGap\relax
        }%
        \setlength{\dgsColophonLift}{%
            \dimexpr\dp\dgsColophonBox + \dgsColophonFootGap\relax
        }%
    }
    (@ set colophon_base = 'answers' if language.booklet.contents.answers
        else 'solutions' if language.booklet.contents.solutions
        else 'problems' if language.booklet.contents.problems
        else 'naboj' @)
    (# **The footer line does not move; the band grows upward.** That is the whole requirement:
        this page should look like the one before it, which means the URL, the page number and
        the e-mail sit exactly where they sit on every other page, with the same air beneath
        them, and the colophon goes in above.

        It cannot be done by making the field taller. LaTeX sets the footer with
        `\baselineskip\footskip`, so its baseline lands `max(\footskip, prevdepth + height +
        \lineskip)` below the text block -- and once the field is taller than `\footskip` (32pt
        here, against about 52pt with a colophon in it) the height term wins and the whole line
        is pushed **20pt** into the bottom margin. The page then has a deeper footer than any
        other and reads as a different page.

        So the field keeps the height it has everywhere -- `\small\thepage` -- and everything
        else hangs above it in a box declared `[0pt][0pt]`, which fancyhdr measures as nothing
        and TeX still draws. The price is that fancyhdr's own rule would then be drawn at the
        *normal* height, straight through the colophon, so this style turns it off and the box
        carries its own: same 0.4pt as `dgs.cls` sets, same `\dgsColophonGap` beneath it as
        there is between the rule and the text on a normal page. Nothing above the footer is
        measured by anyone, which is why `blocks/booklet/footer.jtex` must reserve the room
        with `\dgsColophonRise` -- that reservation is now the only thing keeping the rule off
        the last line of names. #)
    \fancypagestyle{colophon}[(* colophon_base *)]{%
        \renewcommand{\footrulewidth}{0pt}%
        \fancyfoot[C]{%
            \raisebox{\dgsColophonLift}[0pt][0pt]{%
                \makebox[0pt]{%
                    \parbox[b]{\textwidth}{%
                        \centering
                        \rule{\textwidth}{0.4pt}\par
                        \vspace{\dgsColophonGap}%
                        \usebox{\dgsColophonBox}%
                    }%
                }%
            }%
            \small \thepage
        }%
    }
(@ endblock @)

(@ block content @)
    \setcounter{volume}{(* volume.number *)}%
    \pagestyle{naboj}

    (@ if language.booklet.contents.intro @)
        \thispagestyle{first}
        \vspace*{8mm}
        \input{build/(* module.id *)/(* competition.id *)/(* volume.id *)/languages/(* language.id *)/intro.tex}
        \newpage
    (@ endif @)

    (@ if language.booklet.contents.problems @)
        \section{(* i18n[language.id].section.problems *)}
        \pagestyle{problems}
        (@ for problem in volume.problems @)%
            (@ include 'blocks/problem.jtex' @)%
        (@ endfor @)
        \newpage
    (@ endif @)

    (@ if language.booklet.contents.solutions @)
        \section{(* i18n[language.id].section.solutions *)}
        \pagestyle{solutions}
        (@ for problem in volume.problems @)%
            (@ include 'blocks/solution.jtex' @)%
        (@ endfor @)
        \newpage
    (@ endif @)

    (@ if language.booklet.contents.answers @)
        \section{(* i18n[language.id].section.answers *)}
        \pagestyle{answers}
        (@ for problem in volume.problems @)%
            (@ include 'blocks/answer.jtex' @)%
        (@ endfor @)%
    (@ endif @)%
    (@ include 'blocks/booklet/footer.jtex' @)
(@ endblock @)
